==Dutch==

===Etymology===
Etymology uncertain. Earliest documentation with its current meaning from 1622. Van der Sijs claims it's a loanword from Low German, whereas de Vries claims it's related to {{cog|dum|rūsen|tr=causing commotion}}, from which also stems [[geroezemoes]].

Compare also {{cog|de|Rausch}}.

